>     D_κ has J-D0's gauge form ⟺ ϑ_t = 1 for every t ⟺ D_κ = id.  (L983–986)

The displayed biconditional, and the proof that follows it, establish
co-extensiveness for the **gauge-form** failure only. For the **type** failure
the proof says *"For the type clause, one frame suffices: K = F₃, e₁ = 2,
i(κ) = 1, η = 2, μ = 2"* — one frame establishes the existential ("D_κ is not
type-preserving as a family"), not the claimed biconditional, whose unproved
direction is "ϑ live ⟹ some residual changes type at that frame". Symmetrically,
the flat opening clause ("D_κ does **not** preserve the factorization type") is
false where ϑ is dead, since D_κ = id there; only the "co-extensive" rider
rescues it, and that rider is the unproved part. I believe the missing direction
is true (I checked μ = 2 in both parities: odd q, scaling the constant slot by
λ ≠ 1 breaks the discriminant character since a non-identity affine map cannot
preserve the QR character; even q, it breaks Tr(a/b²) since u ↦ Tr((1+λ^{−1})u)
is a nonzero functional) — but the note proves neither, and nothing in the fold
consumes it. Flagged because the round's own CRITICAL was an over-stated
displayed clause of exactly this shape.

### m5 (minor) — §7(f) and WZ-BOX-7 contradict each other, and §7 records no ledger effect for the round's own corpus finding

> So BOX-2's perimeter is neither inherited, enlarged, **nor invoked**, and
> WELD-ZERO adds no consuming site to it. **This note says nothing about the
> other sites that do consume it.**  (L1082–1083)

WZ-BOX-7, added by the same round, says something quite specific about two of
them: GENHN:736–737 and GENH4:370 are both on the weld-face audit's list of ten
sites *"all routing correctly through J-D0 with the type-preserving bijection
exhibited inline"* (`WELD_FACE_AUDIT.md`:193–202), and the box establishes that
