form. The box even quotes the audit's CLEAN-list entry —

> which the weld-face audit's CLEAN-site list reproduces as a correctly routed
> J-D0 site  (L1141–1144)

— but flags only *"the two sites"* (the two frozen notes) for erratum, not the
audit entry that misclassifies them, and §7, the section headed "CONSUMPTION
IMPACT (exact ledger effect, IF the arc accepts)", carries **no row** for any of
it. What r1 discovered is a live corpus-consistency item — two CERTIFIED notes
and one audit inventory state a reason that is false at live ϑ, and the only
correct replacement reason currently lives in this 0/2 note — and the "exact
ledger effect" section does not record it. The fold's own conclusions are
